## ❓ Business Questions Answered

| # | Question | Key Finding |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | How many items were sold in a year? | **5,510 units** across 1,000 transactions (avg 5.51/invoice) |
| 2 | Which product line has max quantity sold per city? | Yangon: Home & Lifestyle · Naypyitaw: Food & Beverages · Mandalay: Sports & Travel |
| 3 | Which product line has minimum quantity sold? | **Health & Beauty** (854 units) — lowest demand overall |
| 4 | Correlation between Unit Price and Quantity? | **r = 0.011** — No meaningful relationship |
| 5 | Sales report for every product line? | Food & Beverages = top revenue ($56K); Health & Beauty = lowest ($49K) |
| 6 | Standard deviation of Quantity and Unit Price? | Qty: σ = 2.92 · Unit Price: σ = $26.49 |
| 7 | Relationship between Quantity and Unit Price? | **r = 0.011** — Confirmed: price does not drive purchase quantity |
| 8 | Relationship between Rating and Gross Income? | **r = −0.036** — Spending level does not affect satisfaction |
| 9 | Relationship between Rating and Quantity? | **r = −0.016** — Basket size has no influence on ratings |
| 10 | Comprehensive Analytics Dashboard | 12 analytical views consolidated in one unified Power BI dashboard |

