## 💡 Overall Conclusions

- The supermarket shows **balanced performance** across all 3 cities and 6 product lines
- **No strong correlations** exist between pricing, quantity purchased, and customer satisfaction
- Customer satisfaction appears driven by **service quality and store experience** — not transaction value
- **Food & Beverages** leads in revenue and customer rating; **Health & Beauty** needs targeted promotional attention
- The **wide price spread** (σ = $26.49) confirms a diverse product catalogue serving varied customer segments

